  "case_against": "The mechanism and the universe contradict each other. The bot is named NEWLIST-BREAKOUT and the theory says the edge exists because 'recently listed assets trend hard... supply is still locked' with a regime of 'first years after listing' (submission.theory.mekanisme, submission.theory.rezim) — but the universe is NEARUSDT and ATOMUSDT (submission.spec.universe), both established assets that appear in the incumbent 16-asset universe (fabius_bots.B1-TREND.universe). Neither the mechanism, the counterparty story, nor the cited TSM reference explains why a 20-day breakout on two old mid-caps should persist; the reference supports generic momentum, not new-listing supply dynamics. The submission's declarations also do not reconcile with the measured record: the submitter claims Sharpe 1.5 and +40% annual (submission.evidence.klaim) versus measured +1.10 and +31% (gates.G3.value, gates.K1.value) — the Sharpe sits exactly at the K4 tolerance edge and the return claim is ungated; the submitter declares 3 trials (submission.evidence.percobaan) while the registry records 12 (stage1.n_trials); and the declared in-sample of Jan-Aug 2025 plus a 2-month OOS (submission.evidence) cannot be reconciled with a 1104-day PnL record (gates.G2.value) whose start and end dates are not stated. Statistically the edge is fragile: dropping the best year cuts Sharpe from +1.10 to +0.21 (gates.G7.value), the placebo upper bound is 0.049 against a 0.05 bar (gates.G8.value), and only 24 signals exist in 3 years, 7.9/year (gates.K3.value). The book is two assets, flat 78% of days (attribution.share_days_flat_pct), capacity is unmeasured (gates.G11.status = NA), and 70% of active days are net long with 0.7 correlation to the equal-weight universe (attribution) — much of what is measured looks like concentrated long crypto beta.",
